Changelog: 20-11-2026 12:22:43

Added. tools/clean_caches.py removes what the development tools leave on the computer, and tools/ci-local.sh runs it before every run (owner, 20-11-2026: "make it a service or feature or script or whatever that does this automatically"): a ci-local venv no run used for a week (tools/ci_local.py marks the ones it uses; a venv from before the marks gets one and stays), pytest's files in /tmp of runs a day ago or longer, an AI assistant's scratch folders in /tmp without a change for six hours, and container images without a name. It reports the system's crash dumps from 1 GB on, with the command that removes them. /tmp is kept in memory on Bazzite: 3.7 GB of such files left the computer short of memory, and the kernel killed the portal's tests in a ci-local run for it. ./test.sh and tools/all_tests.py --run keep no files of a test that passed. PCSX2 Manager's tests remove theirs however pytest was started (apps/pcsx2/tests/conftest.py): its memory cards are 8 to 64 MB each, 1.1 GB a run; the cards are not made smaller, as 8 MB is the smallest card a PS2 has and the tests check the real sizes. The wiki's development page says so.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 12:03:07

Fixed. The cache of the runner packages (.github/actions/runner-packages) is one per week and per Ubuntu release, no longer one per runner image. GitHub's runners were on four images in one run, so the plan job filled the cache of its own image only and the jobs on the other three downloaded the packages themselves: the step took 29 seconds per job on average and 118 at most, against 9 seconds from the cache. A new week's cache starts from the week before. tools/ci-apt.sh gives the first try 20 seconds, not 60, before it takes the next mirror: Azure's mirror gave 109 kB/s where the next one gave 26 MB/s.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 10:42:42

Fixed. The CI jobs no longer download the same packages from Ubuntu's mirror each (owner, 20-11-2026: "every test has to download that same font over and over"): Bazzite's font and the libraries Qt needs, which the Ubuntu 26.04 runner lacks (ten packages per job), are downloaded once, by ci.yml's plan job, and kept in GitHub's cache (.github/actions/runner-packages, tools/ci-apt.sh); the pytest and docs jobs and docs.yml install them from the cache with tools/ci-qt-libs.sh and tools/ci-font.sh. Some runners reach the mirror at about 45 kB/s, and their jobs failed at the step's 5 minutes before a test ran; cutting a try off after 45 seconds did not help there. A download is now tried three times, each try going on where the last stopped, the second and third from the next mirror in the runner's list. Dependabot also reads the action; a change to .github/actions/ or to tools/ci-apt.sh runs every job.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 10:32:13

