Changelog: 18-11-2026 16:41:03

Added. tools/text_check.py lists what is wrong with the text people read (owner, 18-11-2026: "also add the
text_check"). It reads the wiki, the READMEs, the text in the apps' windows, the portal's texts in portal/apps.toml
and the messages the apps' scripts print. It checks the text against the writing standard in .claude/writing.md,
with LanguageTool (spelling, grammar and American English, in a podman container) and with Vale (style and
readability, the rule sets in tools/text_check/styles/). It is no test and no CI check. In Claude Code,
/rewrite-text rewrites the text with it and checks every changed sentence against the code. The owner's decisions on
the text are in .claude/text-decisions.md. The tool came from its twin. The badge check
(tools/tests/test_readme_badges.py) leaves out the READMEs of the pinned Vale styles, which are their makers' own
files.

