English voice with the Kokoro model on the machine itself, and saves the speech as an Ogg Vorbis, MP3, FLAC or WAV
file. Nexus Dashboard has its tile, and its installer test is tools/installer-tests/text.sh. The root
requirements-dev.txt takes in its requirements, which add numpy and soundfile for its tests. The wiki's Dashboard
chapter describes it under Text to Speech. Its speech engine has a venv of its own outside the checkout, set up from
the app's window, because onnxruntime has no wheel for the dev venv's Python. The app came from its twin, where the
owner tried it first.

