Changelog: 17-11-2026 21:35:50

Fixed. SFTP Tools' test of the error dot counted the log's handlers, and a window an earlier test left behind
took its own away in the middle of it: the test failed, and the run then crashed, whenever pytest wrote a report
(--junitxml, as tools/all_tests.py --run does). It follows the window's own handler now. The windows a test of SFTP
Tools opens are closed and deleted when it ends: left to Python's garbage collector, windows of earlier tests were
taken apart during a later test, which is what crashed the run.

